{"profile":{"name":"Amber Morley","ward":"Ward 3, Etobicoke—Lakeshore","bio":"Amber Morley was elected to represent Ward 3, Etobicoke-Lakeshore on October 24, 2022, defeating incumbent Mark Grimes with 46.44% of the vote. Before council she spent over 20 years in community advocacy, including as Director of the South Etobicoke Youth Assembly at LAMP Community Health Centre, as an Administrative Assistant to Councillor Peter Milczyn, and as a Constituency Assistant for Ward 4 Etobicoke-Centre. She also serves as a non-statutory Deputy Mayor for Etobicoke and York, appointed August 2023.","committees":["Etobicoke York Community Council","Executive Committee","Infrastructure and Environment Committee","Budget Committee","FIFA World Cup 2026 Subcommittee","Toronto Police Services Board","Long-Term Care Committee of Management","Confronting Anti-Black Racism Advisory Committee (Chair)","Toronto Public Library (Mayor's designate)"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_morley@toronto.ca","phone":"416-397-9273"},"promises":[{"text":"Push for a set standard of affordable units in all new housing developments, and lend support to new co-operative housing initiatives.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Utilize city-owned land for affordable housing developments, and work with other levels of government to leverage provincial and federal lands.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Commit to a Vacant Home Tax to discourage speculative buyers.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":377,"term":377,"first":"2022-11-16","last":"2026-09-03","lobbyists":80,"clients":83,"subjects":157,"methods":{"Meetings":101,"Emails":243,"Phone calls":9,"Written":9,"Other or unreported":15},"top":[{"label":"Affordable Housing","count":77},{"label":"Economic Development","count":73},{"label":"Planning and Development, Combined Application","count":59},{"label":"By-law / Reg